  "body": "## What and why\n\nAdd the three missing test pins from #3145:\n\n- A cross drill enters `turn_of` through `posed_kind`. An axial drill does not.\n- `table_top` reads `PosedTurn::Line` with a displaced origin and a non-unit tilted axis.\n- The posed verdict alone refuses `Face1` with the complete first-traverse diagnostic. The index-swing clause does not mask it.\n\nThe last test builds its machine inline. It states the rotary clearances and uses a synthetic long-flute cutter. Only one verdict blocks the low-clearance case. Changing only the clearance removes that verdict and posts the control program.\n\nThe two unit tests join the existing private test module. The posting test joins the existing integration binary. Existing safety assertions remain intact. The decision is in `docs/decisions/3145-posed-traverse-pins.md`.\n\n## Checks on the final head\n\nEnvironment: Linux, Rust 1.100.0, existing worktree and caches. `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_SWEEP=off`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: PASS, four real steps. The app library passes 316 tests. `first_traverse_posed` passes eight. `first_traverse_table_tilt` passes six.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test first_traverse_rotary`: PASS, three neighboring controls.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --lib --test first_traverse_table_tilt --test first_traverse_posed --test first_traverse_rotary -- -D warnings`: PASS.\n- `git diff --check`: PASS.\n- Runtime preservation: the complete source prefix before `#[cfg(test)]` is byte-identical to the base. `posting.rs` is unchanged.\n\nNamed new tests:\n\n- `operation::first_traverse_posed::tests::a_cross_drill_enters_the_posed_law_but_an_axial_drill_does_not`\n- `operation::first_traverse_posed::tests::the_fixed_table_reads_a_single_rotary_line_in_the_paths_height_scale`\n- `the_posed_verdict_alone_refuses_the_post_by_operation_name`\n\n## Sensitivity checks\n\nEach temporary mutation makes its named test fail:\n\n- Remove the cross-drill branch from `posed_kind`: the cross drill no longer receives `PosedTurn::Line`.\n- Replace the line origin with zero in `table_top`: the tilted height is wrong.\n- Omit `FirstTraverseLow` from the warnings sent to the post: the unsafe test program posts, so `expect_err` fails.\n\nAll mutations were restored. The final quick gate and strict clippy pass after restoration. No mutation is committed.\n\n## Scope and limits\n\nThis is test-only coverage, not a change to a safety law. No runtime geometry, collision, simulation, machine asset, example, golden or G-code implementation changes.\n\nNot run: the light lane, full application/workspace, catalog, GUI, release or heavy builds. The repository asks for the light lane at review. This contribution's authorized proportional scope excludes that broad release build; it is **not run**, not a pass. No post or toolpath implementation changed, so catalog suites are not selected. No physical-machine certification is claimed.\n\nThe stock simulation explicitly does not judge the control program's posed moves. The test proves the existing first-traverse and posting clauses, not full material-simulation acceptance.\n\nThe initial fixture exposed stock shank warnings. The final synthetic cutter clears that stock without deleting warnings or disabling checks. An initial attempt to call a private helper did not compile; the test now uses the public verification gate.\n\nA maintainer approves and merges this contribution. No merge or auto-merge is requested.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #3145\n",
